---

## Lore

Voodoo, the magical faith carried to the Americas by people of African descent, is not the evil cult the word is often used for. Its priests - houngans if male, mambos if female - are protectors of their communities and use their magic for the common good. Evil Voodoo priests exist but are rare, shunned, and sometimes hunted down by the good. In the Kingdom of Bahia they are the backbone of the island''s defense, able to call up whole armies of loa spirits.

The class shares much with Rifts Africa''s African Priest. With the Game Master''s permission a Voodoo priest may know some of the rituals and ceremonies from Rifts Africa (pages 86-91); if so, he knows only three spells at first level and one per level after. The Medicine Man and Rain Maker, and the evil African Witch and Necromancer, can also be found among Voodoo practitioners, as described in that book.

## Starting Weapon

30% of Voodoo priests start with an energy weapon and 1D4 spare E-clips, 30% with a bio-weapon, 30% with a Techno-Wizard weapon, and 10% with one energy weapon plus a Techno-Wizard or biomancy weapon. The priest also carries candles, incense and a stick of chalk among the ceremonial tools, and 2D4x1000 credits'' worth of saleable herbs and teas.
', 'published', 'data-script'
